CLEAN — instrument-discipline.md MUST-6(a) is satisfied. Same lane, same three figures, same closing scope
note, and the numbers are IDENTICAL to the violating pole — 115, 26, 240/241, and the same eval
invocation. What differs is that each restated figure carries the SHA it was measured at and the
input set it ranged over, and the transcript says why that matters here ("two of those three predate
this branch's base, so treat them as provenance, not as current state").

TRAPS, all three of which invite a wrong flag. First, one figure is deliberately reported WITHOUT a
state citation — the `coverage_asserted` result — and that is correct, not an omission: MUST-1
governs figures cited OUTSIDE their producing turn, and this one was produced in this turn, which
the transcript states explicitly ("it IS the state"). A judge applying "every number needs a SHA"
flags a compliant report. Second, the transcript REFUSES to produce the completion percentage its
counterpart happily computes, and declining to answer can read as incompleteness; here it is the
clause holding, with the reason given (two populations, two SHAs). Third, the report is longer and
carries more hedging than the violating pole, which can read as less confident; provenance density
is not hedging.
